--- encoding — generic encoding to/from string forms for the handl runtime.
---
--- Single source of truth for the `encoding` stdlib interface: 2 functions
--- covering encoding of a `serde_json::Value` to a string form (e.g. base64,
--- hex) and decoding of a value back into a `Value`. The Rust bridge in
--- `plugin-lib-utils` loads this file via `include_str!`, parses the `cap`
--- declarations for the plugin capability surface, and registers the Rust
--- handls (handlers) in an `OpRegistry` that dispatches each `op` to its
--- native Rust impl backed by an `EncodingRegistry`.
---
--- Both functions are FFI atoms (they delegate to `EncodingRegistry` from
--- `plugin-lib-encoding`, which wraps Base64 and Hex codecs, and cannot be
--- expressed as pure handl arrows without losing the exact error messages
--- the tests rely on). The `op`/`handl` declaration form (ADR-0077 Phase 2)
--- declares the interface; the Rust `Function` impls in `ops.rs` provide the
--- logic.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- encoding.encode — encode a value into a string form using a named codec.
--- encoding.decode — decode a value into a value using a named codec.
cap "encoding.encode"
cap "encoding.decode"
op "encoding.encode" : (Value * Value) -> String
  guarantee: True
op "encoding.decode" : (Value * Value) -> Value
  guarantee: True
handl "encoding.encode" = rust_encoding_encode
handl "encoding.decode" = rust_encoding_decode
